usage: metric_scope_vorbereiten.py [-h] --scope SCOPE --output OUTPUT
                                   --tf-probe TF_PROBE --install-root
                                   INSTALL_ROOT [--timeout TIMEOUT]
                                   [--map-owner MAP_OWNER]
                                   [--manager-owner MANAGER_OWNER]
                                   [--odom-owner ODOM_OWNER]

Bind a private, explicitly reviewed LAB polygon to the current passive stack.
Reads /map, MapManager status, TF and ROS graph ownership. Starts only the
existing native read-only TF provenance observer, never Explorer or a mission.
The printed existing Explorer launch stays passive and conservative.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --scope SCOPE         private explicitly reviewed LAB-scope JSON
  --output OUTPUT       new private YAML outside repository
  --tf-probe TF_PROBE   built existing tools/simulation/tf_ownership_probe
                        binary
  --install-root INSTALL_ROOT
                        explicit product-install root; reject mixed/old Python
                        overlays
  --timeout TIMEOUT
  --map-owner MAP_OWNER
  --manager-owner MANAGER_OWNER
  --odom-owner ODOM_OWNER

Scope JSON needs schema_version=1, session_id, scope_id, frame_id, current
map_fingerprint, accessible_scope_verified=true and explicit vertices
[[x,y],...]. Read the fingerprint from the current
/robot_map_manager/status_json; never reuse a prior map epoch blindly.
